<!--
  MachineBlocks — concept documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept.TransformationConcepts
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbt="com.machineblocks.bml.type">

  <name>TransformationConcepts</name>
  <type>concept:TransformationConcepts</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MachineBlocks transformation concepts</is>

  <documentation>
    Geometry and children are built first in local space, then transformed together. After the
    local build, the effective order is:

    direction → align → rotationOffset → rotation → rotationOffsetRevert → offset

    direction — semantic 90° grid orientation (west / north / east / south). At north and south,
    size X and Y swap for placement; face semantics stay west-local for authoring.
    Prefer direction over free rotation whenever the intent is grid-aligned reorientation.

    align — start / center / end relative to the reference bounding box (studs, slope, bevel, and
    crop do not change the align box). alignChildren sets the parent origin used by children
    (default start on all axes).

    rotation — free rotation after alignment; not grid-safe; last resort.
    rotationOffset — optional pivot for rotation; may be reverted after rotation.
    offset — final placement translation only.

    Face identifiers in V3 are strings ("x-", "x+", "y-", "y+", "z-", "z+"), not integers.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="concept:StructureSystems" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — body, underside, enclosure, and connection structure.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:Direction" relation="Defines">
      Semantic grid orientation enum.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:Align" relation="Defines">
      Alignment enum used by align and alignChildren.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:OffsetXYZ" relation="Defines">
      Placement offset compound type.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:RotationXYZ" relation="Defines">
      Free rotation compound type.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:NativeBlock" relation="Defines">
      SSOT for direction, align, alignChildren, rotation, rotationOffset, offset.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
